John D. C. Little, Are There “Laws” of Manufacturing?, in Manufacturing Systems: Foundations of World-Class Practice, edited by Joseph A. Heim and W. Dale Compton, National Academy of Engineering, National Academy Press, 1992, DOI 10.17226/1867. The [publisher's chapter](https://www.nationalacademies.org/read/1867/chapter/22) provides authorized online reading.

On 1 November 2026, the [front matter](https://www.nationalacademies.org/read/1867/chapter/1) and actual pages 180–181 were inspected for attribution and the area argument, including its explicit end-effect/limit qualification. Read the complete chapter progressively; the whole book and its empirical examples were not audited. The original trace extension here is not published observational data.

The front matter states copyright 1992 National Academy of Sciences and restrictive reproduction terms. Free online reading is not an open-content licence. Link externally; no book pages, figure or source media are copied. The trail supplies its own finite-window proof, numbers and programs.
